From 6f6a6d0f2ac492363f99380cb2ee990c82308869 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:14:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(preloader): Signal Storm, a studio-poster boot adapted
 from the waving landing

AD[I]TYA / H[I]MAONE share one giant I (a tall bar that doubles as a
playhead); a storm of studio words (PLAY, REC, LOOP, MIX...) in the lane colours
shutters away as the letters roll into place like slot reels; the poster thumps,
rules draw, labels decode, two pads slide in, and a metronome rises and ticks at
120 BPM; then three track lanes shutter open onto the page (2.8s).

Glyph engine ported from the reference into poster-glyphs.ts; hash and the
timecode decode extracted to preloader-kit.ts and shared with Signal Lock.
Overlay only (fixed, inset-0, contain: strict, pointer-events-none), one
STORM_TIMELINE feeding the CSS, separate reduced-motion composition. LandingGate
now plays it; SignalLockPreloader is a one-line swap.
